COMPREHENSIVE MASTER COMPENDIUM FOR FIH COMMUNITY 
This document serves as the comprehensive technical standard, administration manual, and official operational guide for the entire FIH Community ecosystem. This dossier has been fully updated and expanded to detail all sub-systems of the Web Portal architecture, the Geometry Dash level system (Fish List), server governance regulations, the TeMoney economy, the jail system, and the Zombie Apocalypse survival game module.
1. ECOSYSTEM OVERVIEW & WEB PORTAL ARCHITECTURE
The FIH Community ecosystem operates on an integrated platform for players, level creators, verifiers, and Geometry Dash community members. The system consists of two core operational layers:
	•	FIH Web Portal (Baseline v2.4.1): A Single Page Application (SPA) built on React 18, Tailwind CSS, and local state management (localStorage storing fih_submissions and fih_collabs). The website is responsible for managing level verification submissions, creator profiles, collaboration tools, the Helper search network, and hall-of-fame leaderboards.
	•	FIH AGENT Discord Bot (Coded by Jery - SEF Team): A server management automation bot written in Python (discord.py library). The bot handles economy management, stock/crypto markets, Black Cat Loans credit, moderation processing, automated correctional jail tasks, and the Zombie survival game module.
Web Portal Functional Modules (v2.4.1)
	•	Dashboard (Home): Integrates a global search bar for players, levels, or collab projects. Displays a list of recently verified levels with embedded YouTube preview videos, level IDs, estimated difficulties, and reward points (e.g., Oceanic Void - ID: 1012345, 500 pts; Cyber Pulse - ID: 1056789, 350 pts; Glacial Peak - ID: 1098765, 480 pts). The Main Server Spotlight section honors the Rank #01 project (The Eternal Void). The User Statistics corner tracks Total Points and total verified levels.
	•	Community Portal (Join Discord): Provides official community conduct rules and a direct invitation link to join the Discord server.
	•	Submit Level: Geometry Dash achievement submission form including fields: Level Name, Level ID, Estimated Difficulty (Easy Demon to Extreme Demon), Proof Video URL, and Creator Notes.
	•	Creator List: Hall of Fame honoring top builders, decorators, and optimizers. Examples: AquaFlow (Master Decorator - 1250 PTS), NeonStrike (Layout King - 980 PTS), Xenon (Lead Optimizer - 750 PTS).
	•	Collaboration Hub (Collab Host): Dual-view mode allowing users to browse open collab slots or use a host approval dashboard (Accept/Reject).
	•	Find Helper Network: A noticeboard connecting creators with specialists across 3 roles: Decorator, Playtester, and Builder.
	•	Fish List & Other List: The official level ranking system categorized by difficulty and prestige points.
